  "notes": ["The October 2026 U.S. label separates safety populations. Among 2,799 single-agent recipients in pooled melanoma and lung-cancer trials, hypothyroidism occurred in 8% (237/2,799) and adrenal insufficiency in 0.8% (22/2,799). Those are not TNBC-specific rates. In KEYNOTE-522, 778 people received pembrolizumab with the perioperative strategy, and adverse reactions led to its discontinuation in 20%. Immune-mediated reactions can begin after stopping treatment. For neoadjuvant TNBC use, the label calls for blood cortisol monitoring at baseline, before surgery and when clinically indicated; these labelled monitoring instructions are separate from a prediction of individual benefit or harm."],
