    tldr: "A Chinese bispecific that beat Keytruda head-to-head on progression-free survival in lung cancer; its maker says it is the first drug to do so in a phase 3 trial.",
    summary: "HARMONi-2 (China): PFS 11.1 vs 5.8 months versus pembrolizumab in PD-L1+ first-line NSCLC at a planned interim analysis; an interim overall survival analysis presented in September 2026 also favoured ivonescimab (hazard ratio 0.73, 95% CI 0.57 to 0.95), as reported by Summit. Approved in China for EGFR-mutant NSCLC after TKI (May 2024, HARMONi-A), first-line PD-L1+ NSCLC (April 2025) and, with chemotherapy, first-line squamous NSCLC (August 2026, HARMONi-6). Summit Therapeutics holds Western rights; HARMONi (global, EGFR-mutant post-TKI) met PFS but OS was not statistically significant in 2025, and on 15 November 2026 Summit announced that the FDA had issued a complete response letter on the US application built on it, because there was no statistically significant overall survival improvement; it is not approved in the US. HARMONi-3 (squamous and non-squamous first-line) ongoing. Spawned a wave of PD-(L)1×VEGF bispecifics (Pfizer/3SBio, BMS/BioNTech, Merck/LaNova).",
